    "question": "Bert, Ernie, and Peggy collect stamps.  Bert has four times as many stamps as Ernie, but Ernie has three times as many stamps as Peggy.  If Peggy currently has 75 stamps in her collection, how many stamps does she need to add to her collection to have a collection as large as Bert's collection?",
    "gold": "825",
    "answer": "Ernie has three times as many stamps as Peggy, or 3*75=<<3*75=225>>225 stamps.\nBert has 4 times as many stamps as Ernie, or 4*225=<<4*225=900>>900 stamps.\nThus, Peggy would need 900-75=<<900-75=825>>825 more stamps to have a collection as large as Bert's.\n#### 825"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many stamps Peggy needs to add to her collection to have as many stamps as Bert, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the number of stamps Ernie has:**\n   - We know that Ernie has three times as many stamps as Peggy.\n   - Peggy currently has 75 stamps.\n   - Therefore, Ernie has:\n     \\[\n     3 \\times 75 = 225 \\text{ stamps}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Determine the number of stamps Bert has:**\n   - Bert has four times as many stamps as Ernie.\n   - Ernie has 225 stamps.\n   - Therefore, Bert has:\n     \\[\n     4 \\times 225 = 900 \\text{ stamps}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the number of stamps Peggy needs to add:**\n   - Peggy currently has 75 stamps.\n   - To have as many stamps as Bert, she needs:\n     \\[\n     900 - 75 = 825 \\text{ stamps}\n     \\]\n\nThus, Peggy needs to add \\(\\boxed{825}\\) stamps to her collection to have as many stamps as Bert.",
